        "orario": "12:44",
        "timestamp": 1776336259,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Netanyahu will speak with Lebanese president Aoun, Israeli minister says On the ground Issued on: 16/04/2026 - 12:44 Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu will speak with Lebanese President Joseph Aoun on Thursday, according to Israel's Minister for Innovation, Science and Technology Gila Gamliel. US President Donald Trump had said the \"leaders\" of Israel and Lebanon would speak for the first time on Thursday, in what would be a historic first. Gamliel's statement was the first confirmation from an official Israeli source that talks would take place. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem. China condemns US Hormuz blockade as oil flows Disrupted 16/04/2026 Pope urges Cameroon's leaders to examine 'conscience', tackle corruption 16/04/2026 French MPs to debate antisemitism law that critics say will stifle criticism 16/04/2026 France father who confined son in van faces 30 years in jail 16/04/2026 Pakistani army chief visits Tehran in hopes for renewed talks between US and Iran 16/04/2026 Ukraine: At least 16 killed in overnight Russian strikes 16/04/2026 Madonna announces new album, a sequel two decades later, 'Confessions on a Dance Floor: Part II' 16/04/2026 Trump says Lebanese and Israeli leaders to speak 16/04/2026 Lebanon expresses cautious optimism on US president's claim of direct talks with Israel 16/04/2026"
